{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested — ordinary review of I2 base milestone at exact head 50bba45ca68ed5b43fa46a5ec79ed1c171261260, invitation 7a70c02a, original efb4e323/ef7febce. Reporting artifact 947feb34 is first and all 148 standing subjects are reviewed. Three supported P2 findings remain. This milestone does not complete I2 or W1–W5.\n\nP2 — Decode nested receiver-local items in admitted record fields. packages/derive/src/handlers.ts:63–67 converts a message's item references through lists but not records. A receiver R has an existing non-genesis card opened at q, and admits a handler with payload: record {about: item of card}. Another admitted lane S declares the corresponding member as a fact of R's opening kind/definition, receives the exact verified R.q evidence and sends that record. The repaired recursive wire preserves its full foreign fact reference. On R, bound finds the handler, but messageRead leaves payload.about as a FactRef; values.ts:47,54 requires a local ID and refuses the valid message as bad-field. The equivalent direct item field works, including the opening-hash check, in forms-handlers.test.ts:162–163. Recursively convert admitted record/list members by their declared types, preserving scope/incarnation/opening hash/item-type checks. Use the existing small message-form fixture for the valid nested item and wrong-reference distinction. This is a pre-existing receive gap exposed by the recursive wire repair, not an introduced regression or the explicitly deferred dotted-member operand feature.\n\nP2 — Preserve the source's field meaning when reading a foreign entry. packages/derive/src/operand.ts:111–116 decodes a fetched foreign delivery with bound(j.definition,...): the reader's definition. An admitted lane A sends tagged to S with tag:{self:true}, declared as a record containing a boolean member. S's record-typed handler accepts that record, as DR6 intends. Reader R verifies S's applied delivery as a fact of kind tagged under S, but happens to declare an unrelated tagged handler whose tag is a fact. A valid fact.where equality comparing the foreign tag with the verified A.send reference then follows guards.ts:194–210 → operand.ts:134,116 → handlers.ts:44–50 → fields.ts:208. R's types turn S's record into A.send's FactRef, so equality passes and a guarded effect can be admitted on the wrong evidence. It should fail: S admitted a record, not that reference. validate/guards.ts:179–182 permits this whole-field comparison; no dotted operand or future capability is involved. Interpret a foreign field from the referenced entry and its own source semantics, rather than unrelated reader declarations; retain the legitimate boolean-self record and actual self-mark distinction. Add a cheap existing fact/field-form witness showing that unrelated reader handlers cannot change a foreign field or its guard result. Adopted53 record semantics at 1882–1885 and the field-part table at 2340 support this requirement. This is incorrect guard evidence, not a claimed general grant bypass.\n\nP2 — Preserve the public target-chain depth budget during settlement. packages/replay/src/verify.ts:348 advances an owing run from depth zero, while Limits.depth at line 52 and README:135 define foreign facts followed in a chain from the target. Use the existing histories(true) fixture at test/verify.test.ts:41–71, target T, no anchors, depth=1: T.1 proves S.1 at depth one; S's missing text triggers settlement at depth zero; S.2 proves U.1 at depth one even though U is the second foreign scope from T. With S.3/U.2 tombstones clearing all owed texts, the code permits consistent past the caller's stated maximum. Preserve the dynamic owed-scope closure repair while carrying the appropriate target ancestry into settlement and applying the existing limit. DR4 at deltas:816 honestly discloses the reset and leaves the contract question with R1; that owner decision remains owed. If the owner deliberately chooses another measure, the API/docs/report must state it precisely before claiming that guarantee. No new numeric bound or commission is requested. Global scope, entry and byte limits still hold; I claim no unbounded traversal, actual stack failure or executed witness.\n\nThe five mechanisms in prior verdict 1993412c are repaired statically: own-name pending Maps/Object.fromEntries retain legal __proto__ reservations; typed recursive record/list wire restores earlier local facts; recorded delivery decisions bypass auxiliary dependency fetches while retaining source/routing/exact-send/hash checks; settlement visits newly discovered owing scopes; reply guards stop at the existing canonical depth and both transports normalize guard failure, with binding disposal in finally. DR7 also fixes the named-fact repeat-founding witness. These conclusions remain bounded to their actual paths: source entries and declarations can still be required. Genesis kind is recorded from the pinned definition for applied/refused entries, read directly, and checked against the definition in replay mode. The issue-file manifest case now has source support and a wrong-kind control.\n\nCoverage: all 148 current artifacts were freshly bound to the exact head/path/effective decision. The same assigned readers had personal FULL 744 coverage, verified whole-byte unchanged transfers, then read complete assigned changed-content deltas, all additions/removals/context through EOF and affected current functions. n4 additionally freshly FULL-read all eight changed bodies; n2 freshly FULL-read its six changed bodies; n5 freshly FULL-read the primary and three READMEs. The lock is root's prior FULL read transferred after exact unchanged identity, not n5's fresh read. Collective current whole coverage is 2,036,908 bytes/29,460 LF, with no missing subject or binding/fingerprint mismatch. Root independently checked all current/prior fingerprints, read the primary through all 513 lines and critical current repair/finding paths plus adopted53 paragraphs. Root does not claim a fresh whole-body reread or personal full reading of the entire 744→50bba delta. That complete native delta is 153,269 bytes/1,974 LF, SHA256 dc620bfa988bf5a8c1f62497798f2bced0e6d56dff04738caa380b32cb3ab694; assigned readers cover all 34 changed subjects and n5 the four additional main-merge paths.\n\nArchitecture: shared judges, transactional folds and unchanged canonical lane pins remain sound boundaries, but recursive send/receive interpretation must agree and foreign evidence must preserve source meaning. Security: the repeat optimization retains source authentication; incorrect foreign guard evidence is material, and the documented traversal budget must remain reliable. Production capabilities/authority still fail closed. Simplification: align typed recursive conversions, retain ordinary records named self, and repair the existing depth promise without inventing a second protocol. The initial collect/self hypothesis was withdrawn because that collection reads pre-entry items; dotted record field/slot access remains explicitly deferred, not a new finding.\n\nFull W1–W5, all five capacity dimensions, real authority/hold/git-read/platform peers, 35 sends/33 results publication, all connected browser/device/workspace/proposal/review/landing/publication stories and source/removal outcomes remain owned work. Against immutable main 3dc8492b9bc076bcab800cd0220780c9cda03cdc the three named removals are present: derive/frame.ts, derive/validate.ts and parked/contract/evidence.ts; no restoration of the parked old product is certified. The 177 delta rows keep the fixed 165, later DP5 and DR7 distinct. Adopted R1 53 is the genesis source basis; current R1 7ef has changes-requested verdict a7f1c108 and is not adopted. Adopted R3 7bc and C2 167 retain separate implementation/operational duties.\n\nNonblocking: correct stale revision12 “not adopted” language, and say no additional dependency entry/text is read on a repeat because the source